edit: the keys (^ is Ctrl; M- is Esc then the key, or Alt with it)

^G         this help                  ^L          the screen drawn again
^O         save, asking the name      ^S          save
^R         open a file                M-,  M-.    the file before, after
^X         close the file (the last one: edit ends)
^W         find                       M-W  M-Q    find again, backwards
M-R        replace (y, n, a: all)     M-G         go to a line ($: the last)
M-A        mark: a block's start      M-6         copy the line, or block
^K         cut the line, or block     ^U          paste what was cut
M-U        undo                       M-E         redo
arrows  ^B ^F ^P ^N   move            Home End  ^A ^E   a line's start, end
PgUp PgDn  ^Y ^V      a page          M-\  M-/    the text's start, end
Del  ^D    delete                     Backspace   rub out
Tab        a tab (stops every 8)      M-I         auto-indent on, off
M-X        the help lines on, off

^K again and again cuts lines into the cut buffer together.  A file whose
lines end CR LF keeps them so.  Ctrl-C does nothing here.

A key, to go on.
